{"type":"reasoning","id":"446b5f53-4147-4813-9131-92508e5861e7","text":"I've confirmed the O(n²) behavior costs 11.6 seconds for 6000 messages, and since pruning happens before the SSE stream begins, the client would sit in silence that whole time—not fatal but worth flagging. I'm also noticing the usage token calculation now uses a new estimator that appears to inflate numbers 2-3x, which is a hidden coupling I need to trace through to see how usage is actually computed and whether tests cover it.\n\n","timestamp":1791993094138,"session_id":"6aafd459-5304-42f1-9d2a-89b85e0b56ad"}
